1. LINENUM-IO-MODES placeholder:
   Replace with actual line number after `grep -n "io_modes" rk_hdmirx.c`.
   The audit (docs/RK3588_KERNEL_AUDIT.md §3) estimates ~1100-1150.

2. Index hash placeholder (0000000):
   Replace with `git diff` output after applying the change. Run:
       cd /data/company/project/linux-kernel-rockchip-work
       <apply the change>
       git diff drivers/media/platform/rockchip/hdmirx/rk_hdmirx.c

3. Test before sending:
   make ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- -j$(nproc) modules
   v4l2-compliance -d /dev/video0 -s
   v4l2-ctl --device /dev/video0 --stream-dmabuf=4 --stream-count=30

4. checkpatch.pl --strict before format-patch.

5. Upstream coordination:
   - Subscribe linux-media list, check Collabora MR !21 status
   - Cross-link to KVM main RELEASE.md mention of this patch

6. Risk:
   DMA_ATTR_FORCE_CONTIGUOUS removal may affect capture paths if the
   HDMI-RX DMA engine strictly requires physically contiguous memory.
   RK3588 hdmirx DMA uses descriptor rings → supports scatter-gather,
   but real hardware test on NanoPC-T6 is mandatory before commit.
